{
  "id": "privacy-pseudonymization-opt-in",
  "kind": "optional",
  "summary": "Opt-in consumer-local pseudonymization with encrypted scoped mappings, provider approvals and protected history; managed PII Shield requires a Business or Enterprise Platform plan. Ordinary SDK use remains unchanged.",
  "howTo": "For self-managed pseudonymization explicitly set privacy.policy.required: true on the chat handler and privacy.local.required: true on the runtime, with the shield, mapping store, keyring, scope and provider registry. For managed use set privacy.managed: true on createGlirastes and supply a durable scoped state store and fixed stateEnvironmentId (GLIRASTES_STATE_ENVIRONMENT_ID, from the optional Business/Enterprise Citadel privacy block or explicit glirastes connect --privacy --dotenv .env) before live signed bootstrap; either an explicit stateStore factory or fixed UUID opts into managed bootstrap even after removing the privacy object; retain both and restore a missing UUID on privacy_state_binding_mismatch; ordinary pairing never adds a binding; a signed protected policy always enforces protection. Missing or false required does not activate local pseudonymization. Self-managed configuration provides no Platform assurance. Protected mode fails closed, blocks screenshot originals unless explicitly allowed, withholds expired history and oversized results, and refuses memory, result handles, direct commands, tool middleware, approval subject/list lookups, opaque intentRouter/guardrails callbacks and mention markers. Model-input debug hooks and lossy history compaction are disabled in protected turns. Credentials, mappings and raw content remain in the consumer infrastructure. View-context contracts alone do not send context. GID speech remains available only while protection is off; its local STT integration is a separate follow-up. See the privacy reference for migration and acceptance boundaries.",
  "skill": "integrating-glirastes-nextjs",
  "adoptedWhen": {
    "patterns": [
      "required: true",
      "managed: true"
    ]
  },
